{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): sorry, sorry doctor, the auto got stuck near silk board in the rain. we are late only.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): arre, nobody is angry. sit, both of you, catch your breath, the fan is on.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I told her the lift was dead, madam, and then she was on the phone about some serial. I don't even know the story.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (PATIENT): Mm. that serial. umm, I don't know, doctor, where to even start.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): start wherever it is sitting. what is on your mind today?",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (PATIENT): my husband went to a blood camp at the office. they told him he has thalasemia trait. I am pregnant, and I am scared for the baby. I don't know, doctor, what it means.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): we will go slowly. how many weeks are you, if you remember?",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. the last scan they said twenty two weeks, I think. sometimes I say five months and then I get mixed up.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (CAREGIVER): the camp slip is in my bag, doctor. they wrote carrier, thalasemia trait. he had no leave, so I came with madam.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): good that the slip is here. were you ever tested for thalassaemia yourself?",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): no. first time someone is even saying this word to me. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (NURSE): ma'am, quick one before I go. her bp just now is one twenty eight over eighty four, pulse ninety two, saturation ninety eight percent. she climbed the stairs.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): thank you, sister. any bleeding, any leaking of water, pain in the tummy?",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (PATIENT): No bleeding. No water coming. Pain, no. baby is kicking, that much I know.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): kicking is a good sign. what tablets are you taking these days?",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (PATIENT): umm. amlodipin for the pressure, ten, no, twenty milligram, in the morning. the cholesterol one at night, ten milligram, I don't remember the proper name, doctor. sugar tablets, glycomet, five hundred milligram, morning and night. and only the ayurvedic powder in the morning, one teaspoon, amma sent it from the village.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): right. stay on the amlodipin and the glycomet, same doses, don't stop them for this visit. the powder, I would rather you keep it aside, we don't know what is mixed in it.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): amma will not like it. but okay, I can leave it. I don't know, doctor, if that powder was even doing anything.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (CAREGIVER): she has taken that powder since the wedding, every morning, with warm water. the other strips I see them finish, so those she takes.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): trait means he carries one quiet gene, he himself is not ill with thalassaemia. the baby is a worry only if you also carry it. today I simply cannot say which way it is.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (PATIENT): so maybe the baby is fine? I am not sleeping properly, I walk in the hall at night. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): maybe, and that is why we test. any fever, any giddiness, swelling in the feet?",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (PATIENT): Fever no. giddiness no. feet get a little puffy in the evening, after I stand.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): let me see. eyes are not pale, both feet have a little swelling, tummy is soft, the uterus feels about right for twenty two weeks, and on the doppler the baby is nice and steady.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (PATIENT): steady is good, no? I was thinking something is wrong inside.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): steady is good. today itself I want a blood count and an hplc for haemoglobin, to look for the trait in you. sister will draw it once we finish. I will book genetic counselling for this week, and ask your husband to come if he can get an hour off.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (NURSE): hplc and cbc, I will collect after this. counselling desk is free thursday morning, I can put the name down.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): thursday is perfect, book it. and you come back to me in two weeks, with both reports, we will sit and read them together.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (PATIENT): two weeks. if the report is bad, then what? I don't know, doctor. I will bring the camp paper.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): if you are also a carrier, the counsellor will walk you through choices, nothing is decided in a panic today. if only he carries it, the baby is usually fine. bring the original camp paper, not a photo.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (CAREGIVER): it is in the brown folder, I will not misplace it. I will tell him about thursday.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): you came when you should. sister will take the blood now, and I will see you in two weeks."
 ],
